2026-07-07 21:34:09,851 | AGENT | ProjectCoordinator Agent answered: Our company, Faber IA, will employ a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure to manage the project. The phases include Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run. Given the client's specific needs as an accounting and statutory-audit firm, the framing phase will pay particular attention to confidentiality, existing production tools, and seasonality of workload.

We will allocate a dedicated team consisting of a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead to ensure all aspects of the project are adequately covered. The security compliance lead is shared but will prioritize this project's requirements. Additional resources for change management and training will be made available as needed.

To address confidentiality, GDPR compliance, and sovereignty, we will utilize our partnership with OuraneCloud, a French sovereign cloud provider that is SecNumCloud-qualified, ensuring data hosting within the EU without any transfers outside the EU. Data will be protected through encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant.

Our solution, Atelier, is designed to forge document-grounded AI assistants from an organisation's own documents, ensuring that each assistant answers from a controlled corpus and cites its sources, thereby maintaining reliability and traceability of outputs.

Key milestones include:
- Completion of the framing phase with a thorough understanding of the client's environment and requirements.
- Design phase concluding with a detailed solution architecture that integrates with the firm's production tools via API-type interfaces.
- Pilot phase deployment on one office or mission line to test the solution under real conditions before progressive generalisation.
- Generalisation phase with full deployment across all offices or mission lines, accompanied by comprehensive change-management support and training.

Risk mitigation plans involve:
- Regular joint steering committee meetings (monthly) and operational committee meetings (fortnightly) to monitor progress and address issues promptly.
- Utilization of a RACI matrix to formalize roles within the project team and ensure clear accountability.
- A documented escalation path for any unforeseen issues that may arise during the project.
- Continuous monitoring of GDPR compliance, data sovereignty, and confidentiality measures throughout the project lifecycle.

By following this structured approach and leveraging our existing capabilities and partnerships, we aim to deliver a high-quality solution that meets the client's requirements while ensuring the preservation of professional secrecy, reliability of figures, and compliance with all regulatory and environmental constraints.
